{
  "manufacturer": "Janitza",
  "manufacturer_slug": "janitza",
  "model": "UMG 605-PRO power quality analyser (Modbus RTU / Modbus TCP)",
  "model_slug": "umg-605-pro",
  "short_model": "UMG 605-PRO",
  "aliases": [
    "UMG605-PRO",
    "UMG 605PRO",
    "UMG605PRO",
    "Janitza UMG 605"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Power meter (power quality analyser)",
  "applies_to": "UMG 605-PRO from firmware release 5.028, per address list 1.038.009.7.h (09/2022).",
  "summary": "The UMG 605-PRO is a Janitza power quality analyser with an RS-485 port and network (IP) settings. Measurements are big-endian 32-bit floats; the 19000-19120 'frequently required readings' block holds volts, amps, power, CosPhi, frequency, energy and THD, the same block as other Janitza meters. Its other address blocks differ from the UMG 604-PRO, so this map lists the 605-PRO's own addresses for the fourth channel, consumed energy, digital I/O, energy resets, transformer settings and network values.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU",
    "TCP"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 2,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "Addresses are printed as the protocol address and sent unchanged: 19000 is requested as 19000. The list starts at address 0 (system time), which only fits 0-based numbering. In a 1-based or Modicon tool enter 19001 / 419001."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": "Release 5.028 and higher",
  "source": {
    "title": "Power Quality Analyser UMG 605-PRO - Modbus-address list and Formulary (firmware rel. 5.028 and higher)",
    "doc_number": "1.038.009.7.h",
    "revision_date": "2022-09",
    "url": "https://www.janitza.com/files/download/manuals/current/UMG605-PRO/janitza-mal-umg605pro-en.pdf",
    "pages": "Transfer parameters, byte order p. 5; frequently required readings p. 12; main values pp. 14-15, 17; other values pp. 40-41; energy p. 48"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Byte order: the list says its addresses return data big-endian (high byte first, high word in the lower register = ABCD). Adding 32768 to an address returns the same value little-endian; that mirror block is not listed.",
    "Do not reuse UMG 604-PRO addresses outside the 19000 block: on the 605-PRO the main values, energy and settings sit at different addresses (e.g. consumed energy total 6508 instead of 9851).",
    "Access: only the 19000-19716 area carries an RD/WR column (the measured values there are RD). Elsewhere the list has no access column; only the delete commands ('1 = delete') are given write access here.",
    "Left out: 19068 (consumed L1-L3 on tariff 1 only); the consumed total is at 6508 (_WH_V[4]).",
    "Left out: 19636 (_PF_TOTAL) because its printed remark runs into the 'internal temperature' text of the row above, so the row is unclear.",
    "Left out: serial number, Modbus address, RS-485 mode and baud rate (6856-6868), which the list marks 'only for internal use', plus harmonics, min/max/mean, event and display settings.",
    "Measured values refresh every 200 ms."
  ],
